# UI and accessibility

Full direction in `docs/spec/01-design-system.md`. Read it before creating a component.
See `docs/spec/ADAPTATIONS.md` for stack path differences (Prisma, single app).

## The direction in one line

A controlled document, not a dashboard: title blocks, revisions, typed verdicts, 2px radius, cool
drafting-stock surfaces, ink-on-paper contrast, one saturated signal colour used sparingly.

## Non-negotiables

- **Tokens only.** Every colour, radius, spacing and font from `styles/tokens.css` / `app/globals.css`.
  If a value you need doesn't exist, propose adding a token — do not inline it.
- **Spacing scale is 4 / 8 / 12 / 16 / 24 / 32 / 48.** Nothing else.
- **`--radius: 2px`.** Never `rounded-lg`, `rounded-xl`, `rounded-full` except on avatars and chips.
- **`--signal` (survey pink) appears only where a human decision is required**, and on the active link
  in the Evidence Chain. If it exceeds roughly 2% of a screen, cut it back.
- **Every numeral is tabular.** `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` on any score, count or date.
- **Verdicts render glyph + label + wash.** Never colour alone.
- **A statutory gap is not an amber.** `<StatutoryFlag/>` is visually distinct from `at-risk`.
- **`<TitleBlock/>` is the same component on screen and in the PDF cover.** Do not fork it.

## Accessibility — WCAG 2.2 AA is a release gate

- 4.5:1 body contrast, 3:1 large text and UI boundaries.
- 3px `--focus` outline with a 1px `--focus-shadow` inner ring. Never removed.
- 24×24px minimum target size.
- Every flow completable by keyboard. Org graph's accessible peer is `<OrgTable/>`.
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` respected by chain rail, index delta and D3 force simulation.
- Visible persistent labels. Never placeholder-as-label.
- `lang` follows the EN/CY toggle.

Run axe-backed e2e before merging UI changes when practical.

## Component conventions

- Server components by default. `'use client'` only for graph, chain rail, forms, command palette.
- Product domain components live in `components/product/`.

## Motion budget

One orchestrated moment: the index delta. Plus the chain rail slide. Nothing else animates.
